        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: تربة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تربة — turba — \"soil; earth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "التربة هنا جيدة للقمح. at-turba hunā jayyida li-l-qamḥ. The soil here is good for wheat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تربة (turba) is built on the native Arabic root t-r-b, \"earth, dust\" (Lane). It shares its root with turāb, \"dust, soil\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
